  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project 6 of Enhancing Human and Operational Capacities of Somalia&apos;s Immigration Authorities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In order to improve security at its porous and vast borders, the Federal Government of Somalia (FGoS) is aiming at strengthening the capacity of the Immigration and Naturalisation Directorate (IND) in line with the National Development Plan. The programme, started in 2013, focuses on enhancing service delivery and migration functions of Somalia&#x2019;s immigration authorities through improved human and operational capacities. Similar to its 2020-2021 predecessor, the proposed intervention aims to contribute to achieving advancing well-being of society and migrants through stronger migration governance and development. This project aims to achieve this by continuing to foster an integrated approach that focuses on the active engagement of diasporic actors to transfer knowledge and competencies to the IND. Furthermore, it will contribute to the construction of the new IND Kismayo (Branch 2). It will focus organizational and human capacity building at the centralized level of the FGoS in Mogadishu and its Regional Branch in Kismayo.</narrative>
  </description>
